%C - draw into the Raspberry Pi firmware framebuffer (HDMI)

Syntax:
%C [-w width -h height] [-b depth] [-n]

Options:
   -w width    Ask the firmware for this framebuffer width  } both needed;
   -h height   Ask the firmware for this framebuffer height } default: keep
               the mode the firmware set up for the monitor
   -b depth    Ask for this many bits per pixel (16, 24 or 32)
   -n          Do not wait for Enter before exiting

The framebuffer is obtained from the VideoCore firmware through the mailbox
property channel; no graphics driver is involved. The demo draws in whatever
mode the firmware actually grants. The Pi 5 firmware keeps the monitor's
native resolution at 16 bits per pixel regardless of what is asked for.
